{# templates/remnanode-caddyfile.j2
   Rendered to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile from what FCP served (the ingress of the
   bootstrap answer): one `handle` per route to its loopback Xray inbound,
   every other path falls through to the decoy site.

   The site has TWO addresses: the origin hostname (Caddy issues its
   certificate, HTTP-01 on port 80) and a catch-all `https://`, so an edge that
   sends its OWN hostname as SNI and Host (Cloudflare in `full` mode) is still
   answered: `fallback_sni` serves the origin certificate for an unmatched SNI,
   and the catch-all routes the foreign Host. Nothing makes that certificate
   valid FOR the foreign name; which provider modes that suits is recorded in
   FCP (docs/edges.md "Node role contract (Ansible)").

   Members' addresses never reach Xray: each reverse_proxy removes the
   headers in remnawave_caddy_strip_request_headers, its own X-Forwarded-For
   included (header_up runs after Caddy sets the X-Forwarded-* headers, and on
   WebSocket upgrades too). Never set trusted_proxies or client_ip_headers here.
#}
{
    email {{ remnawave_caddy_email }}
    fallback_sni {{ origin_hostname }}
}

{{ origin_hostname }}:{{ caddy_listen_port }}, https://:{{ caddy_listen_port }} {
{% for r in caddy_routes %}
    @r{{ loop.index }} path {{ r.path }}
    handle @r{{ loop.index }} {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{{ r.port }} {
{% for h in remnawave_caddy_strip_request_headers %}
            header_up -{{ h }}
{% endfor %}
        }
    }
{% endfor %}
    handle {
        root * {{ remnawave_decoy_root }}
        file_server
    }
}
